course: dictionary
lesson: 16185
title: Informal words and speech
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Yucky is an informal word. People use it in everyday talk and in stories with real speech, but not usually in formal writing such as a school report. It means very unpleasant or disgusting, especially to taste, touch or look at. «The soup tasted yucky.» The word shows the speaker really does not like it.
explain: Context helps you work out what yucky means. «Sam stepped in the yucky mud and squelched all the way home.» Mud that squelches is messy, and Sam is not happy about it, so yucky must mean disgusting to touch. Check by swapping in disgusting: the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The sound word «yuck!» is what people say when something is disgusting. «Yuck!» is often said with a scrunched-up face. Yucky and yuck belong to the same family of words, and both show strong dislike.
fact: Yucky is an adjective, and its forms are yucky, yuckier and yuckiest.
fact: Yucky means very unpleasant or disgusting, especially to taste, touch or look at.
fact: Yucky is informal, so it is best used in speech, stories and friendly writing, not in formal reports.
fact: «Yuck!» is a sound word that people say when something is disgusting.
fact: A good check is to swap in a formal word such as disgusting or unpleasant and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The medicine was yucky, so Mia held her nose.» What does yucky mean here? | *Very unpleasant to taste | Very sweet and sugary | Bright and shiny | Cold and wet
exercise: Ben looks in the bin and says, «Yuck!» What does this tell you? | *He really dislikes what he sees | He is looking for his bag | He is very tired and wants to sleep | He is very happy with the bin
exercise: Yucky is an informal word. Which word would suit a school report best? | *unpleasant | yuck! | yuckier | yucky
test: «The yucky sock smelled so bad that I held my nose.» What does yucky mean? | Freshly made | Very tasty | Very big | *Very disgusting
test: Which sentence uses yucky correctly? | The yucky sunshine made the garden bright | I won the race and felt yucky | *Yuck, there is a slug in my salad! | Yucky, the bus is on time
exam: In «The yucky mud squelched and splashed on Mia's shoes», what does yucky tell us about Mia? | The mud is dry and dusty | She loves the mud | She is cold and tired | *She finds the mud disgusting
